= Action Plans for Mild to Moderate Cases
<ch:action-mild-moderate>

This chapter addresses patients with mild to moderate ME/CFS who retain some functional capacity but experience significant symptom burden that impairs quality of life. The goal is to maximize function, prevent progression to severe disease, and pursue recovery.

*Note:* For pediatric and adolescent patients, see Chapter @ch:pediatric-ambulatory for age-specific protocols including school accommodations, developmental considerations, and pediatric dosing modifications.

#roadmap(title: [How to Use This Chapter])[
*For patients*: read the severity-stratified pathways section to place yourself, then the immediate-mild-moderate and disease-modifying sections to build a staged plan you can follow at home; for age-specific pediatric protocols, school accommodations, and pediatric dosing, use Chapter @ch:pediatric-ambulatory.

*For caregivers*: use the severity-stratified pathways and work-study sections to help the patient schedule activity within their capacity while preventing progression to severe disease.

*For clinicians*: read the severity-stratified pathways, septad-screening, disease-modifying, and GET-avoidance sections to construct a staged treatment plan that maximises function and prevents progression.

*For researchers*: the septad-screening and disease-modifying sections identify the early-intervention targets where progression to severe disease might be prevented — a key open question for trials.
]

